# Platform Helpers

- Use `SupportedPlatform` (`'win32' | 'darwin' | 'linux'`) from
  `src/shared/types/platform.ts` for all platform types.
  Never use `NodeJS.Platform`.
- Use `currentPlatform()` from `src/shared/utils/platform.ts` for runtime
  platform checks. Never `process.platform` directly.
- Use `PlatformDisplayName` (`'Windows' | 'MacOS' | 'Linux'`) for user-facing
  display and wire format. Convert via `platformDisplayName()` /
  `displayNameToPlatform()`.
- `currentPlatform()` normalizes (never throws) — anything that isn't
  `'win32'` or `'darwin'` maps to `'linux'`.
